returned_finding_id	P1-retained-v7-raw-entry-still-importable
returned_finding	v9 still imports runV7 from the retained v7 module. That v7 module continues to export runV7({authority,evidenceRoot,runCommand}), which accepts a caller-supplied target and invokes Docker/psql without the v9 sealed intake. The statement that v7 cannot be selected by v9 without source modification does not prevent a direct import and invocation of v7 by a Docker-capable caller.
impact	The legacy trust boundary is documented but not enforced; the previously returned raw-execution bypass remains reachable outside executeV9.
required_correction	Remove/export-block the raw v7 executor, or relocate it to a non-importable private implementation and make every executable path perform the current sealed authority intake. Add an import-level regression showing the old module cannot produce child/Docker calls without all current immutable GO inputs.

returned_finding_id_2	P2-v9-candidate-contract-incomplete-and-registry-not-complete
returned_finding_2	At review time no v9 candidate authority, candidate manifest, or handoff exists at the task research paths, so no immutable chain binds runner/spec/registry/future DB-QA-drain-resource reviews. Further, the registry lists E/F containers and volumes but omits known E/F database identities jinhu_b2c197_e and jinhu_b2c197_f; absence checks can accept their reuse.
impact_2	No runnable v9 authority can be reviewed, and the claimed complete historical resource exclusion is not proven for all four identity fields.
required_correction_2	Create immutable v9 authority/manifest/handoff that bind runner, spec, complete registry, DB, QA, drain, and resource GOs. Add all historical E/F database IDs (and independently reconcile every retained run/container/database/volume against authoritative resource artifacts) before binding the registry SHA.
status_after_review	NO-GO-for-resource-create-or-execute; v9-remains-safe-static-placeholder-only
